From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Subject: mfd: core: a cell of a non-DMA parent points its dma_mask at its own zero mask
Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

An MFD cell of an I2C or SPI parent inherited a NULL dma_mask pointer, and a
cell with a device-tree node then triggered a "DMA mask not set" warning.
Point the cell's dma_mask at its own (zero) coherent mask, which is the
state the core produced anyway.

---
diff --git a/drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c b/drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c
--- a/drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c
@@ -173,6 +173,15 @@ static int mfd_add_device(struct device *parent, int id,
 	pdev->dev.dma_mask = parent->dma_mask;
 	pdev->dev.dma_parms = parent->dma_parms;
 	pdev->dev.coherent_dma_mask = parent->coherent_dma_mask;
+	/*
+	 * A parent on a bus without DMA (an I2C or SPI client) has no dma_mask, and its
+	 * cells are no DMA masters either. Point the child's dma_mask at its own (zero)
+	 * coherent mask: that is exactly what of_dma_configure_id() coerces a NULL
+	 * dma_mask to (drivers/of/device.c), so the result is unchanged, without the
+	 * "DMA mask not set" warning that is meant for DMA masters a bus forgot.
+	 */
+	if (!pdev->dev.dma_mask)
+		pdev->dev.dma_mask = &pdev->dev.coherent_dma_mask;
 
 	ret = regulator_bulk_register_supply_alias(
 			&pdev->dev, cell->parent_supplies,
